Date: Sat, 6 Jun 2026 15:27:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 20/31] fix(verimark): Phase 10.3.a async block was inside the
 wrong #ifdef branch
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The async transport block (ctrl_out_async / ctrl_in_async /
transceive_async + finishers) was inserted between the #else stubs and
the existing #endif of the original `#ifdef VERIMARK_HAVE_LIBGUSB / #else
/ #endif` split. It therefore got compiled only when libgusb is NOT
available — the opposite of what we want — and the libfprint link
failed with "undefined reference to verimark_transceive_async" because
the symbol wasn't in transport.c.o at all.

Close the original block right after the last stub, then re-open a
dedicated `#ifdef VERIMARK_HAVE_LIBGUSB` around the async section. No
content change ; the existing trailing `#endif` now closes the new
block.

Drafted with AI assistance.
---
 libfprint/drivers/verimark/transport.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libfprint/drivers/verimark/transport.c b/libfprint/drivers/verimark/transport.c
index 2eaa146..f5d322e 100644
--- a/libfprint/drivers/verimark/transport.c
+++ b/libfprint/drivers/verimark/transport.c
@@ -150,8 +150,11 @@ VerimarkResult verimark_ctrl_in(VerimarkUsbHandle *h,
     return VERIMARK_ERR_TRANSPORT;
 }
 
+#endif /* VERIMARK_HAVE_LIBGUSB (closes the original sync impl / stubs split) */
+
 
 /* === Phase 10.3.a — async transport (libgusb-backed) ================== */
+#ifdef VERIMARK_HAVE_LIBGUSB
 
 /**
